related enum for valid values"} {:number 31, :name "last_exit_reason", :type :enum, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataCV.CvBridgeExitReason", :constraints {:defined-only true}, :description "See related enum for valid values"} {:number 32, :name "bridge_uptime_ms", :type :int64, :constraints {:gte 0}, :description "CV bridge uptime in milliseconds"} {:number 33, :name "restart_count", :type :int32, :constraints {:gte 0}, :description "CV bridge restart count"} {:number 40, :name "roi_focus_day", :type :message, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataROI", :description "ROI edge in NDC (-1.0 to 1.0)"} {:number 41, :name "roi_track_day", :type :message, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataROI", :description "ROI edge in NDC (-1.0 to 1.0)"} {:number 42, :name "roi_zoom_day", :type :message, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataROI", :description "ROI edge in NDC (-1.0 to 1.0)"} {:number 43, :name "roi_fx_day", :type :message, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataROI", :description "ROI edge in NDC (-1.0 to 1.0)"} {:number 50, :name "roi_focus_heat", :type :message, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataROI", :description "ROI edge in NDC (-1.0 to 1.0)"} {:number 51, :name "roi_track_heat", :type :message, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataROI", :description "ROI edge in NDC (-1.0 to 1.0)"} {:number 52, :name "roi_zoom_heat", :type :message, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataROI", :description "ROI edge in NDC (-1.0 to 1.0)"} {:number 53, :name "roi_fx_heat", :type :message, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataROI", :description "ROI edge in NDC (-1.0 to 1.0)"} {:number 60, :name "sharpness_metrics_day", :type :message, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataSharpness", :description "Focus sharpness metric"} {:number 61, :name "sharpness_metrics_heat", :type :message, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataSharpness", :description "Focus sharpness metric"} {:number 70, :name "camera_transform_day", :type :message, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataTransform3D", :description "See [[proto/ser.JonGuiDataTransform3D]]"} {:number 71, :name "camera_transform_heat", :type :message, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataTransform3D", :description "See [[proto/ser.JonGuiDataTransform3D]]"} {:number 80, :name "tracked_objects", :type :message, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataTrackedObject", :repeated true, :description "See [[proto/ser.JonGuiDataTrackedObject]]"} {:number 90, :name "trinity_tracking_active", :type :bool, :description "Whether the Ring-Trinity board tracker is **running**. It follows the tracker's actual run state, which [[proto/cmd.CV.StartTrackTrinity]] and [[proto/cmd.CV.StopTrackTrinity]] are what change.\n\n**This is the STATE plane's answer, and it exists for the toggle affordance.** A consumer reading `JonGUIState` can enable, disable and reflect the trinity control from this field alone; it never has to decode `JonGUIState.opaque_payloads`, which the state plane does not parse.\n\n**The pose travels on the other plane, to a different consumer, and this field does not serve it.** [[proto/ser.TrinityTracking]] rides `JonGUIState.opaque_payloads` and is routed to the OSD overlay, which renders the metric pose. That consumer needs the pose, the per-axis sigmas, the observability figures and the board identity — a bool would tell it nothing. The two are not copies of one another and neither suppresses the other: different contracts, different consumers, different evolution boundaries.\n\n**It collapses the tracker's states on purpose.** `LOCKED`, `SEARCHING`, `DEGRADED` and `BOARD_MISMATCH` are all `true` here, because a toggle asks only whether tracking is RUNNING; `TRINITY_TRACKING_STATUS_IDLE` is `false`, as is the tracker not being up at all. Anything that must tell those apart — is there a lock, is the pose valid, is this the board that was asked for — reads `TrinityTracking.status` ([[proto/ser.TrinityTrackingStatus]]) from the opaque payload, which is the authoritative and richer value. This field cannot answer that and must not be read as though it could.\n\nIt carries no validation constraint, and none is available: `false` is proto3's zero default, so nothing on the wire distinguishes \"not tracking\" from \"this field was never populated\". That is the same absence-versus-state hazard [[proto/ser.TrinityTrackingStatus]] documents one plane over, and it is why this field answers the toggle question only, rather than standing in for the tracker's health."} {:number 91, :name "zoom_roi_active_day", :type :bool} {:number 92, :name "zoom_roi_active_heat", :type :bool}], :oneofs [{:name "_roi_focus_day", :required false, :fields [40]} {:name "_roi_track_day", :required false, :fields [41]} {:name "_roi_zoom_day", :required false, :fields [42]} {:name "_roi_fx_day", :required false, :fields [43]} {:name "_roi_focus_heat", :required false, :fields [50]} {:name "_roi_track_heat", :required false, :fields [51]} {:name "_roi_zoom_heat", :required false, :fields [52]} {:name "_roi_fx_heat", :required false, :fields [53]} {:name "_sharpness_metrics_day", :required false, :fields [60]} {:name "_sharpness_metrics_heat", :required false, :fields [61]} {:name "_camera_transform_day", :required false, :fields [70]} {:name "_camera_transform_heat", :required false, :fields [71]}], :description "CV Gateway state enrichment message: the CV subsystem's per-tick state as it appears on the STATE plane, for both day and heat camera channels.\n\nThis message is populated by the CV Gateway and embedded in `JonGUIState` before being written to shared memory. It provides real-time visibility into:\n- Autofocus sweep progress and state\n- Current and best sharpness measurements, and the sharpness metrics carrying their temporal derivatives\n- The regions of interest each camera operation is using — focus, track, zoom, fx — per channel\n- CV bridge container status, exit reason, uptime and restart count\n- Camera 3D pose and velocity, per channel\n- Tracked objects, each carrying a UUID for joining against external data\n- Whether the Ring-Trinity board tracker is running\n\nThe ROI coordinates use Normalized Device Coordinates (NDC) ranging from -1 to 1, where (0,0) is the center of the frame.\n\n**This message is the STATE plane, and it is not the whole CV surface.** The richer CV output — object detections ([[proto/ser.ObjectDetectionsDay]], [[proto/ser.ObjectDetectionsHeat]]), SAM tracking, the aggregated [[proto/ser.CvMeta]], and the Ring-Trinity metric pose [[proto/ser.TrinityTracking]] — does not travel here. It rides `JonGUIState.opaque_payloads` as [[proto/ser.JonOpaquePayload]] entries and is decoded only by the consumers that handle each payload type, the OSD overlay path among them. A consumer of this message does not parse those payloads.\n\nThat split is why a fact an opaque payload already carries can also appear here, in the reduced form a state consumer can act on — `trinity_tracking_active` (#90) is exactly that shape. The two are different contracts with different consumers and different evolution boundaries; neither is a copy of the other, and neither suppresses the other."}, "cmd.HeatCamera.SetAGC" {:id "cmd.HeatCamera.SetAGC", :name "SetAGC", :package "cmd.HeatCamera", :source "jon_shared_cmd_heat_camera.proto", :fields [{:number 1, :name "value", :type :enum, :type-ref "ser.JonGuiDataVideoChannelHeatAGCModes", :constraints {:defined-only true, :not-in [0]}, :description "See related enum for valid values", :interaction {:semantic-type :enum-label, :presets ["MODE_1" "MODE_2" "MODE_3"]}}], :description "Configures the Automatic Gain Control (AGC) mode for the thermal camera to optimize image enhancement for different viewing conditions. Accepts an enumerated value (MODE_1, MODE_2, or MODE_3) that adjusts how the camera processes thermal intensity for display.", :interaction {:category :settings, :ui-pattern :enum-picker, :feedback :pending-timeout, :purpose "Sets automatic gain control mode for thermal camera image enhancement", :related-state ["ser.JonGuiDataCameraHeat#agc_mode"], :related-commands ["cmd.HeatCamera.NextFxMode" "cmd.HeatCamera.SetFilters"], :preconditions ["Heat camera started"], :notes "Cycles through AGC modes (MODE_1, MODE_2, MODE_3) for different viewing conditions"}}, "cmd.RotaryPlatform.setUseRotaryAsCompass" {:id "cmd.RotaryPlatform.setUseRotaryAsCompass", :name "setUseRotaryAsCompass", :package "cmd.RotaryPlatform", :source "jon_shared_cmd_rotary.proto", :fields [{:number 1, :name "flag", :type :bool, :description "Enable/disable flag", :interaction {:semantic-type :raw}}], :description "Toggles whether the rotary platform's position readings are used as the primary compass heading source. When enabled, the platform's orientation is stored in the `use_platform_positioning` state flag and used by the rotary subsystem to determine heading.", :interaction {:category :settings, :ui-pattern :toggle, :feedback :pending-timeout, :purpose "Enables or disables using rotary platform position as compass heading", :related-state ["ser.JonGuiDataRotary#use_rotary_as_compass"], :related-commands ["cmd.Compass.SetUseRotaryPosition"], :notes "Configuration toggle for compass data source"}}, "ser.JonGuiDataROI" {:id "ser.JonGuiDataROI", :name "JonGuiDataROI", :package "ser", :source "jon_shared_data_types.proto", :fields [{:number 1, :name "x1", :type :double, :constraints {:lte 1, :gte -1}, :description "Left edge in NDC (-1.0 to 1.0)"} {:number 2, :name "y1", :type :double, :constraints {:lte 1, :gte -1}, :description "Top edge in NDC (-1.0 to 1.0)"} {:number 3, :name "x2", :type :double, :constraints {:lte 1, :gte -1}, :description "Right edge in NDC (-1.0 to 1.0)"} {:number 4, :name "y2", :type :double, :constraints {:lte 1, :gte -1}, :description "Bottom edge in NDC (-1.0 to 1.0)"}], :description "Region of Interest (ROI) for CV tracking. Defines a rectangular area in normalized coordinates where -1,-1 is top-left and 1,1 is bottom-right of the frame. Used to specify the initial tracking target or search area for computer vision algorithms."}, "cmd.Gps.Start" {:id "cmd.Gps.Start", :name "Start", :package "cmd.Gps", :source "jon_shared_cmd_gps.proto", :fields [], :description "Starts the GPS module and begins receiving position data. This parameterless lifecycle command initializes the GPS hardware and triggers data collection, typically activated via a power toggle button in the UI.", :interaction {:category :lifecycle, :ui-pattern :action-button, :feedback :fire-and-forget, :purpose "Starts the GPS module", :related-state ["ser.JonGuiDataGps#is_started"], :related-commands ["cmd.Gps.Stop"], :preconditions ["System powered on"], :notes "Lifecycle command to initialize GPS hardware"}}, "cmd.System.WipeUserData" {:id "cmd.System.WipeUserData", :name "WipeUserData", :package "cmd.System", :source "jon_shared_cmd_system.proto", :fields [], :description "Permanently deletes all user data from the device, including all photos, videos, recordings, and custom settings. Requires explicit user confirmation through a modal dialog before execution due to the irreversible nature of the operation.", :interaction {:category :diagnostic, :ui-pattern :action-button, :feedback :fire-and-forget, :purpose "Wipes all user data from the system (factory reset)", :related-commands ["cmd.System.ResetConfigs" "cmd.System.SaveFactoryDefaults"], :preconditions ["User confirmation required"], :notes "Destructive operation, requires confirmation dialog in UI"}}, "ser.JonGuiDataSharpness" {:id "ser.JonGuiDataSharpness", :name "JonGuiDataSharpness", :package "ser", :source "jon_shared_data_types.proto", :fields [{:number 1, :name "value", :type :double, :constraints {:lte 1, :gte 0}, :description "Normalized value (0.0 to 1.0)"} {:number 2, :name "derivative_1", :type :double} {:number 3, :name "derivative_2", :type :double}], :description "Image sharpness metric for autofocus. Contains the normalized sharpness value (0-1) along with first and second derivatives for tracking focus trend. Used by CV algorithms to determine optimal focus position by maximizing sharpness."}, "cmd.Heater.EnableAutomaticControl" {:id "cmd.Heater.EnableAutomaticControl", :name "EnableAutomaticControl", :package "cmd.Heater", :source "jon_shared_cmd_heater.proto", :fields [], :description "Enables PID-based automatic temperature regulation for all heater channels. When enabled, the heater module runs a periodic control loop (default 500ms interval) that computes power output per channel using PID control, comparing current temperatures against targets set via `SetAutomaticControlParams`. Target temperatures and PID gains (kp, ki, kd) are loaded from persistent configuration; this command only activates the control loop. The `automatic_control_enabled` flag in `ser.JonGuiDataHeater` reflects the current state. Use `DisableAutomaticControl` to stop automatic regulation, which also resets PID accumulators and sends zero power to hardware.", :interaction {:category :actuator, :ui-pattern :action-button, :feedback :pending-timeout, :related-state ["ser.JonGuiDataHeater#automatic_control_enabled"], :related-commands ["cmd.Heater.DisableAutomaticControl" "cmd.Heater.SetAutomaticControlParams"]}}, "cmd.HeatCamera.ZoomStop" {:id "cmd.HeatCamera.ZoomStop", :name "ZoomStop", :package "cmd.HeatCamera", :source "jon_shared_cmd_heat_camera.proto", :fields [], :description "Stops the thermal camera zoom motion in progress, sent when the zoom button is released after a zoom in or out command. Used in press-release input patterns for analog zoom control.", :interaction {:category :actuator, :ui-pattern :action-button, :feedback :fire-and-forget, :purpose "Stops continuous zoom movement on heat camera", :related-state ["ser.JonGuiDataCameraHeat"], :related-commands ["cmd.HeatCamera.ZoomIn" "cmd.HeatCamera.ZoomOut"], :preconditions ["Heat camera started"], :notes "Used with continuous zoom in/out commands"}}, "cmd.DayCamera.SetAutoIris" {:id "cmd.DayCamera.SetAutoIris", :name "SetAutoIris", :package "cmd.DayCamera", :source "jon_shared_cmd_day_camera.proto", :fields [{:number 1, :name "value", :type :bool, :description "Enable/disable state", :interaction {:semantic-type :raw}}], :description "Enables or disables automatic iris control for the day camera, allowing automatic aperture adjustment based on lighting conditions. When enabled, manual iris control via SetIris is disabled; when disabled, the operator can manually adjust the iris for precise exposure control.", :interaction {:category :settings, :ui-pattern :toggle, :feedback :pending-timeout, :purpose "Enables or disables automatic iris control for day camera exposure", :related-state ["ser.JonGuiDataCameraDay#auto_iris"], :related-commands ["cmd.DayCamera.SetIris"], :preconditions ["Day camera started"], :notes "When enabled, disables manual iris control"}}, "cmd.RotaryPlatform.ScanDeleteNode" {:id "cmd.RotaryPlatform.ScanDeleteNode", :name "ScanDeleteNode", :package "cmd.RotaryPlatform", :source "jon_shared_cmd_rotary.proto", :fields [{:number 1, :name "index", :type :int32, :constraints {:gte 0}, :description "Zero-based node index", :interaction {:semantic-type :count}}], :description "Deletes a waypoint from the rotary scan pattern at the specified index, updating the current scan node position after removal.", :interaction {:category :actuator, :ui-pattern :number-input, :feedback :pending-timeout, :purpose "Deletes a node from the scanning pattern", :related-state ["ser.JonGuiDataRotary"], :related-commands ["cmd.RotaryPlatform.ScanAddNode" "cmd.RotaryPlatform.ScanUpdateNode" "cmd.RotaryPlatform.ScanRefreshNodeList"], :preconditions ["Scan pattern exists"], :notes "Part of scan pattern editor UI"}}, "cmd.System.SetTimeZone" {:id "cmd.System.SetTimeZone", :name "SetTimeZone", :package "cmd.System", :source "jon_shared_cmd_system.proto", :fields [{:number 1, :name "zone_id", :type :int32, :constraints {:lt 595, :gte 0}, :description "IANA timezone identifier", :interaction {:semantic-type :count}}], :description "Sets the device's timezone using a numeric zone ID (0-594) that maps to standard IANA timezone names (e.g., America/New_York,